# Backend-only Docker image (see Dockerfile) — keep the build context to
# what the Go build and the runtime stage actually need. binaries/ alone is
# ~2.6GB across all platforms; without this file the whole tree would be
# streamed to the Docker daemon on every build.

.git/
build/
build_output/
dist/
dist_packages/

# Flutter desktop frontend — not part of this image (backend-only).
frontend/

# Docs/notes — irrelevant to the image, large in aggregate.
docs/
obsidian-doc/
obsidian-doc-en/
versinNote/

# Only binaries/linux/cpu ships in this image (see Dockerfile). Windows/macOS
# binaries and the GPU (nvidia/amd) llama.cpp variants are unusable in a
# standard container without GPU passthrough the CasaOS target doesn't have;
# ngrok is unused (CasaOS's own port mapping/reverse proxy covers this
# instead); the bundled Whisper STT model is the single biggest file in the
# repo and downloads on demand like any other model, same as a native install.
binaries/windows/
binaries/darwin/
binaries/linux/nvidia/
binaries/linux/amd/
binaries/linux/ngrok
binaries/linux/cpu/ggml-small.bin
binaries/linux/cpu/llama-new/

# Runtime/user data — never baked into the image, always a mounted volume.
# Exception: providers.example.json is a template the Dockerfile itself
# COPYs in (seeded into the volume by docker/entrypoint.sh on first boot,
# same as config.yaml.example) — it has to survive this exclusion. BuildKit
# (what docker/build-push-action's buildx always uses) resolves a later,
# more specific "!" rule against an already-excluded parent directory
# correctly; the classic docker builder does not, but this image is never
# built with it.
data/
!data/providers.example.json
config/config.yaml
.env
